  "description": "Gendron's C, C+ and R instances of the multicommodity capacitated fixed-charge network design problem, as distributed by the CommaLAB group of the University of Pisa. Each instance is a directed network whose arcs carry a variable cost per unit of flow, a capacity and a fixed cost of opening the arc, and a set of commodities, each a demand to route from an origin node to a destination node. In each instance the network nodes are nodes of type node, each commodity is a node of type commodity carrying its demand with an origin edge and a destination edge to the nodes it joins, and the arcs are edges of type arc. The instances carry no reference values; published optima and bounds are in the papers that use the set.",
